      "status": "ok",
      "output": {
        "decision": "answer",
        "reason": "The evidence from paper 1806.09652 fully supports explaining the NMT model and training setup for this topic. The Machine Translation section states that NMT models were trained with the TensorFlow implementation of OpenNMT using an attention-based transformer architecture, and that NMT BLEU scores were higher than SMT scores for both en–ta and en–hi pairs (c-0377bffbf88cf9ead25b03ff, s9-p2). The Conclusion adds that parallel sentence pairs were extracted using a Siamese BiRNN encoder with GRU activation (c-1ef4f6dc83e93c39e90f82dc, s10-p0), and that BLEU improved by 11.03% (en–ta) and 14.7% (en–hi) due to using the extracted pairs (c-1ef4f6dc83e93c39e90f82dc, s10-p2). The Abstract confirms the harvested dataset improved BLEU for both NMT and phrase-based SMT on these low-resource pairs (c-1dd6dc3c2f7d9eb29dc26d9f, abstract). Only conclusions present in these passages are stated; no common-sense additions are made."
      },
